<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        Hardened-runtime entitlements for nox.

        Hardened runtime is required for Apple notarization. By default
        it locks down a lot of behavior; we have to explicitly opt out
        of restrictions we genuinely need.

        ─ App Sandbox is intentionally OFF (no `com.apple.security.app-
          sandbox` key). nox legitimately needs unsandboxed access to:
            • the global event tap (for the Fn-key dictation hold)
            • the menu-bar status item APIs
            • cross-app paste-at-cursor via CGEvent posts
            • dlopen of /System/Library/PrivateFrameworks/MediaRemote
            • Apple Events to query Spotify / Music for timing
          App Store sandbox forbids all of the above; that's why we
          ship direct-download instead. Same path Alcove, NotchNook,
          Sleeve all take.
    -->

    <!--
        dlopen of private frameworks (MediaRemote, in particular)
        requires this on hardened-runtime apps. Without it dyld
        refuses to load any framework not signed by Apple AND
        embedded in the bundle, which kills the whole music HUD.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
        AppleScript bridge for Spotify and Music timing fallbacks
        (the AppleScript-driven `playerPosition` reads). Without
        this, AppleEvents to other apps return errAEEventNotPermitted
        on hardened-runtime builds even after the user grants the
        Automation permission.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
        WhisperKit / swift-transformers ML models load via mmap.
        Some Metal Performance Shaders code paths on Apple Silicon
        legitimately use JIT compilation. Allowing it here keeps
        Local Whisper transcription working on hardened builds.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
        2026-05-06 — REQUIRED for AVCaptureDevice.requestAccess(for:.audio)
        to actually fire the TCC microphone prompt on hardened-runtime,
        unsandboxed apps. Without this entitlement the call silently
        no-ops: no prompt, no log line, no error — just nothing happens
        and the user thinks dictation is broken. Confirmed via Apple
        Developer Forums thread "Audio Entitlements stopped working".

        On sandboxed apps the same key gates mic access at sandbox
        level; on hardened-runtime-only apps (us) it's what tells
        TCC the binary is allowed to even REQUEST microphone access.
        Drop this and 1.9.x's "I tapped Fn and nothing transcribed"
        bug returns.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
